    {
      "id": "seg:paragraph:discussion:0008:0001",
      "source": "Under rare circumstances, the system terminates and restarts its media services daemon.",
      "ko": "세션에서 생성하고 실행하기 전에 [`ARConfiguration`](arconfiguration.md)에서 [`isSupported`](arconfiguration/issupported.md)를 호출하여 지원되는지 확인한 다음 [`runWithConfiguration:`](arsession/runwithconfiguration:.md)로 실행합니다.",
      "sourceHash": "2d951f9a548c0b659b4311986f99933935364e1660db41d7f9679e498df31fcc",
      "status": "machine_translated"
    },
    {
      "id": "seg:paragraph:discussion:0008:0002",
      "source": "Respond to these events by reinitializing your app’s audio objects (such as players, recorders, converters, or audio queues) and resetting your audio session’s category, options, and mode configuration.",
      "ko": "For more information on ARKit’s coordinate space, see [`setWorldOrigin(relativeTransform:)`](arsession/setworldorigin(relativetransform:).md).",
      "sourceHash": "6728be39614bcdca587f732810afe6e62052b1e47376da93a7f39dda3b6e9ed8",
      "status": "machine_translated"
    },
    {
      "id": "seg:paragraph:discussion:0008:0003",
      "source": "Your app shouldn’t restart its media playback, recording, or processing until initiated by user action.",
      "ko": "Your app shouldn’t restart its media playback, recording, or processing until initiated by user action.",
      "sourceHash": "b97b10b4a588799650c24b92977c845e77e75d96f0d33878c8ea9cd5e0a8f9d0",
      "status": "failed"
    },
    {
      "id": "seg:blockquote:discussion:0009:0001",
      "source": "**Note**: You can trigger a media server reset by choosing the “Reset Media Services” selection under the Developer menu in the iOS Settings app.",
      "ko": "**Note**: You can trigger a media server reset by choosing the “Reset Media Services” selection under the Developer menu in the iOS Settings app.",
      "sourceHash": "112b0aec6117c51b295fb9bdbd8f67dd86e8965cf24752a2ef9b7146186e75e7",
      "status": "failed"
    },
    {
      "id": "seg:blockquote:discussion:0009:0002",
      "source": "Using this utility helps to ensure that your app responds appropriately if media services were reset.",
      "ko": "Using this utility helps to ensure that your app responds appropriately if media services were reset.",
      "sourceHash": "0e02f95b37c4a85f92a5ccc6110bb257bad8675a99ff0e10e9281f6194637bca",
      "status": "failed"
    },
    {
      "id": "seg:paragraph:discussion:0010:0001",
      "source": "This notification has no [`userInfo`](https://developer.apple.com/documentation/Foundation/NSNotification/userInfo) dictionary.",
      "ko": "This notification has no [`userInfo`](https://developer.apple.com/documentation/Foundation/NSNotification/userInfo) dictionary.",
      "sourceHash": "21f9d6f4aedcf703ff1455efb6220118483ca5963239233f5ddff4a4c0575102",
      "status": "failed"
    },
    {
      "id": "seg:paragraph:discussion:0011:0001",
      "source": "The system posts this notification on the main thread.",
      "ko": "The system posts this notification on the main thread.",
      "sourceHash": "d0ceb162936c3668e67927d82fb1621ce878c86713bde28d484832cd0f87bfa7",
      "status": "failed"
    },
    {
      "id": "seg:blockquote:discussion:0012:0001",
      "source": "❗ **Important**: Apps don’t need to reregister for any audio session notifications and don’t need to reset key-value observers on audio session properties after a media services reset.",
      "ko": "❗ **Important**: Apps don’t need to reregister for any audio session notifications and don’t need to reset key-value observers on audio session properties after a media services reset.",
      "sourceHash": "2b51af0be55659d65b13dd16b1a9e339286959399b1f4ea562abf8f44b9005ab",
      "status": "failed"
